Task: Fix Skunk varchar/text codec mismatch (Green)

Summary: orders.item and orders.status are Postgres 'text' columns (per the V1/V2
migrations' TEXT column type), but OrderStore's selectOrder query and insertOrder
command declared them with Skunk's varchar codec. Skunk's ParseDescribe step compares
the query's asserted output-column types against Postgres's actual described row and
throws ColumnAlignmentException on any mismatch — this only surfaced now because
get()'s SELECT is the first query in this codebase whose decoder Skunk actually
validates this strictly for (the original INSERT's varchar parameter apparently wasn't
checked the same way, or was checked loosely enough not to fail — either way, text is
the objectively correct codec for a text column, so both were fixed).

